<!-- <html>/<body> are ignored - only <body>'s children are copied into the page. -->
<!--
    Search-box visibility flag placeholder (issue #178).

    Bind this file to the "webhelp.fragment.after.header" placeholder, which is
    included on ALL four generated page types (main/tiles, topic, search
    results, index terms) - including the two that are not built from a topic
    and so carry no edition marker of their own.

    The element below is deliberately EMPTY: xslt/inc/customSearchFlag.xsl
    matches it in `copy_template` mode and either replaces it with the hidden
    `.wh-search-hidden` marker that resources/hide-search.css keys off, or drops
    it entirely, according to the webhelp.show.search scenario parameter.

    The <html>/<body> wrapper is not decoration: Oxygen's includeCustomHTMLContent
    copies only <body>'s children when it finds that wrapper, and copies the WHOLE
    document - these comments included - when it does not.
-->
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
    <body>
        <div class="wh_search_visibility"/>
    </body>
</html>
